<p>Funds were swept out at 13:03 to 13:05 UTC. The USDC on Ethereum went to a <strong>HitBTC deposit address</strong>. The TRON wallet has been in use since <strong>March 2026</strong>, so this actor was active long before this campaign. We cannot see how many cards or cookies reached <code>1688360.cc</code>.</p><h2 id="who-was-affected">Who was affected</h2><p>We fetched <strong>1,611 distinct Optimizely snippets</strong>, found mostly through our own crawl data, and checked each one for the malicious code. <strong>188 snippets belonging to 178 organisations were infected.</strong> We kept a copy of every infected file, along with its response headers, SHA-256 hash and fetch time as evidence. The real number is likely higher as we could only check snippets we could find in time.</p><h3 id="by-sector">By sector</h3><table>
