ge/fetch/$s_!OG7v!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F542f0e5a-b2aa-4857-88e3-09f42f6966fc_800x700.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><span>Now that we have intuition on the geometry, we can move on to some basics of network structure. This will be the final piece of the puzzle before stating our main theorem, the deficiency zero theorem. The first definition we need is the linkage class </span><sup>[2]</sup><span>. For example, Feinberg's first network</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
A &amp;\rightleftharpoons 2B \\
A + C &amp;\rightleftharpoons D \\
D &amp;\to B + E \\
B + E &amp;\to A + C
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>can be drawn graphically with arrows between the complexes:</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png" width="728" height="289.17953165654814" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:458,&quot;width&quot;:1153,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h1Xv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F86809a25-067b-47ba-95ec-19cc7bdfde97_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>If we remove the arrows, the diagram looks like this.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png" width="728" height="289.17953165654814" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:458,&quot;width&quot;:1153,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!3i9M!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F66977828-702b-4dd7-8ae6-a30c1160e652_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><span>The </span><strong>linkage classes</strong><span> are the sets of complexes that are connected, ignoring the direction of arrows. So Feinberg's first network has two linkage classes. The two linkage classes are shown in different colours. The linkage classes are</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\mathcal{L}_1 = \{\,A,\ 2B\,\}, \qquad \mathcal{L}_2 = \{\,A + C,\ D,\ B + E\,\}, \qquad \ell = 2</span></p></div><p>Which graphically look like:</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png" width="728" height="289.17953165654814" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:458,&quot;width&quot;:1153,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>This network</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
A &amp;\rightleftharpoons B \\
B &amp;\rightleftharpoons C \\
C &amp;\rightleftharpoons A
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>has one linkage class because all of the nodes are connected.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png" width="728" height="649.2453825857519" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:676,&quot;width&quot;:758,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7071!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F524b23bb-a240-44c8-bcdd-a91c6b85d5ac_758x676.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>This network has three linkage classes because none of the reactions share a common complex!</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
X &amp;\to 2X \\
X + Y &amp;\to 2Y \\
Y &amp;\to 0
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><div><figure><div data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png" width="728" height="132.02072538860102" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:245,&quot;width&quot;:1351,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RCtD!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4dc7c903-9d69-431f-b2f4-de6be655bdec_1351x245.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></figure></div><p><span>Just like in chemistry, we also have the notion of reversibility in a chemical reaction network. A reaction is </span><strong>reversible</strong><span> if, for all </span><strong>y</strong><span> and </span><strong>y′</strong><span>, if </span><strong>y → y′</strong><span>, then </span><strong>y′ → y</strong><span>. So the following network is reversible, because B reacts to A when A reacts to B.</span></p><p>This network is also reversible, since every species that reacts to another species has the inverse included.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
A &amp;\rightleftharpoons B \\
B &amp;\rightleftharpoons C
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>The following network is not reversible</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
A &amp;\to B \\
B &amp;\to C \\
C &amp;\to A
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p><span>because even though A reacts to B, </span><strong>B doesn't react to A directly.</strong><span>  But it turns out that there is a weaker definition. We say a complex y </span><strong>ultimately reacts</strong><span> to another complex y' if there is a path of complexes such that</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\mathbf{y} \to \mathbf{a}_1 \to \mathbf{a}_2 \to \cdots \to \mathbf{a}_n \to \mathbf{y}'</span></p></div><p>So in this network</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
X &amp;\to Y \\
Y &amp;\to Z
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>we find that X → Y → Z, so X ⇒ Z.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png" width="728" height="354.027397260274" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:497,&quot;width&quot;:1022,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nnHS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0b0460b0-ccda-42f4-bebe-a79f9f8cefeb_1022x497.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>A reaction is weakly reversible if for all y, if y ultimately reacts to y', then y' also ultimately reacts to y.</p><p><span>The reaction below is </span><strong>weakly reversible</strong></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
A &amp;\to B \\
B &amp;\to C \\
C &amp;\to A
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p><span>But it's </span><strong>not reversible</strong><span> because even though A reacts to B, B doesn't react to A.</span></p><p>We now have the idea of a stoichiometric compatibility class and an equilibrium locus. And so for arbitrary kinetics, if we start from a given initial concentration, we know two things.</p><ol><li><p>The concentration will evolve somewhere within the stoichiometric compatibility class, and</p></li><li><p>Equilibrium points will lie somewhere on the locus of equilibrium.</p></li></ol><p><span>This means that for a given starting concentration, </span><em><strong>if</strong></em><span> the </span><strong>concentration vector does converge to a limit</strong><span>, it must converge to a point within the geometric intersection of its stoichiometric compatibility class and the locus of equilibria. Note that it is not necessary that the concentration vector converges to a limit at all; we might have a limit cycle.</span></p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif" width="728" height="637" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/da9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:700,&quot;width&quot;:800,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/gif&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Psld!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda9a7a62-195d-47c7-918e-7ca1edfaad07_800x700.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>Let's try to calculate these intersection points explicitly for a simple network.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>B \xrightarrow{k_1} A, \qquad A + 2B \xrightarrow{k_2} 3B</span></p></div><p>First, calculate our reaction vectors.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>A - B = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}, \qquad 3B - (A + 2B) = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}</span></p></div><p>The reaction vectors span a line. The stoichiometric compatibility classes are therefore the following line segments.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>S = \operatorname{span}\left\{ \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \right\}</span></p></div><p>From the kinetics point of view, mass action kinetics gives</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
\dot c_A &amp;= k_1 c_B - k_2 c_A c_B^{2} \\
\dot c_B &amp;= -k_1 c_B + k_2 c_A c_B^{2}
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>To calculate the locus of equilibrium, we set the left hand sides of this equation to zero. This means that our locus of equilibrium is given by the following plot</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>0 = k_1 c_B - k_2 c_A c_B^{2} \;\Longrightarrow\; c_B = 0 \quad \text{or} \quad c_A c_B = \frac{k_1}{k_2}</span></p></div><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png" width="728" height="709.1007268951195" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:938,&quot;width&quot;:963,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!74_w!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F48a6c327-b1f1-45d1-ab12-702d811f0a7a_963x938.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>Our stoichiometric classes are given by the set of lines parallel to the stoichiometric subspace, which look like the following</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif" width="728" height="672" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:600,&quot;width&quot;:650,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/gif&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_dhy!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f709752-3e27-4273-a770-9d7cf59c02e1_650x600.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>This means that we can either have zero, one or two solutions depending on where the class lies.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png" width="728" height="709.1007268951195" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:938,&quot;width&quot;:963,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mPSb!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4fca27f7-570c-4aab-acce-278dd438fa89_963x938.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><span>We can count the number of equilibrium solutions. The stoichiometric classes can be rewritten as the following, for an arbitrary value of </span><em>T</em></p><p>If we substitute that into our equilibrium locus, we get</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>(T - c_B)\,c_B = \frac{k_1}{k_2}</span></p></div><p>This is a quadratic equation with solution</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>c_B = \frac{T \pm \sqrt{T^2 - 4k_1/k_2}}{2}</span></p></div><p>The concentration can't be imaginary, which means the term in the square root can't be negative. And so for a solution to exist we require that</p><p>And also, T can't be negative since our stoichiometric classes only live in the positive section. This leads us to the only equilibrium condition being</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>T \ge 2\sqrt{\frac{k_1}{k_2}}</span></p></div><p>Solving a quadratic equation is easy. But unfortunately, most network systems are so complex that we can't easily get the number of equilibria. For example, suppose we had the horrible looking mass action kinetic equation</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
\dot a &amp;= k_1 a - k_{-1} a^2 - k_2 a b + k_{-2} c \\
\dot b &amp;= -k_2 a b + k_{-2} c + k_3 c - k_{-3} b \\
\dot c &amp;= k_2 a b - k_{-2} c - k_3 c + k_{-3} b
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>How many equilibria are there in a given stoichiometric class, and what is their nature? It's unclear, and to do this we would have to solve some pretty horrible equations, with little general insight into what makes these systems special. This is where the deficiency zero theorem comes in, and it's the final result of this essay.</p><p><span>The </span><em>deficiency zero theorem</em><span> allows us to make meaningful statements about the number of equilibria in a network, under some conditions </span><sup>[2][28]</sup><span>. The </span><em>deficiency</em><span> of a network is given by its number of complexes, minus the number of linkage classes, minus the dimension of the stoichiometric subspace it has. This is often denoted by the Greek letter delta.</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\delta = \underbrace{n}_{\text{complexes}} \;-\; \underbrace{\ell}_{\text{linkage classes}} \;-\; \underbrace{s}_{\dim S}</span></p></div><p>The deficiency zero theorem says that if we have a deficiency zero network, then two things could happen, based on whether the network is weakly reversible or not.</p><p>If a network is not weakly reversible, then for any kinetics, the system doesn't have a positive equilibrium or a cyclic trajectory where all species concentrations are positive. By positive equilibrium, it means an equilibrium concentration vector in which every element is strictly positive. It still could in theory converge to equilibria where one component is zero.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif" width="728" height="344.1454545454545" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:520,&quot;width&quot;:1100,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/gif&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5SAm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc19254ea-ae0d-4836-961d-0adba371dd84_1100x520.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><span>But suppose it </span><strong>is</strong><span> weakly reversible. Then for mass action kinetics, we have that each positive stoichiometric compatibility class has precisely one equilibrium, that equilibrium is </span><strong>asymptotically stable</strong><span>; and there is no nontrivial cyclic composition trajectory along which all species concentrations are positive.</span></p><p><em><strong>Asymptotically stable</strong></em><span> means that if we start at a concentration point near enough the equilibrium point, then the trajectory of the concentration vector should converge to that equilibrium point. What the statement does not say is whether this is true for an arbitrary concentration point; it is still possible that the concentration doesn't converge at all to either a point or a cycle. The </span><strong>global attractor conjecture</strong><span> however posits that arbitrary starting concentrations will tend to equilibria in the long time limit, but this is still unproven.</span></p><p><span>For example, the reversible monomer to dimer reaction is weakly reversible, has deficiency zero, and so our equilibrium locus only intersects </span><strong>once</strong><span> with our stoichiometric compatibility classes.</span></p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif" width="728" height="644.8" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:620,&quot;width&quot;:700,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/gif&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4SNL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_lossy/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a6b1c04-4e50-46ba-9db5-82c9add633c9_700x620.gif 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>This can be summarised in this tree diagram.</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png" width="728" height="414.80782198246794" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:845,&quot;width&quot;:1483,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FVXq!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47181b8f-3115-4f3a-9f72-44a904b8ec7b_1483x845.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><span>Let's take Feinberg's first toy network </span><sup>[2]</sup><span>. It looks really complicated, and it's not clear at all what equilibria this should have, if any!</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
A &amp;\rightleftharpoons 2B \\
A + C &amp;\rightleftharpoons D \\
D &amp;\to B + E \\
B + E &amp;\to A + C
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>But let's compute the deficiency of this network and see where it can help us. We can count five complexes</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\{\,A,\ 2B,\ A + C,\ D,\ B + E\,\}, \qquad n = 5</span></p></div><p>Our reaction vectors are</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{u}_1 &amp;= 2B - A &amp;&amp;= \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 2 \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \\[1ex]
\mathbf{u}_2 &amp;= D - (A + C) &amp;&amp;= \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \\[1ex]
\mathbf{u}_3 &amp;= (B + E) - D &amp;&amp;= \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \\[1ex]
\mathbf{u}_4 &amp;= (A + C) - (B + E) &amp;&amp;= \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>In our last section on stoichiometric subspaces, we calculated the rank of these reaction vectors by reducing them to row echelon form. We found that the row echelon form only contained three non-zero rows. That means that the dimension of the stoichiometric subspace is 3.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>s = \dim \operatorname{span}\{\mathbf{u}_1, \mathbf{u}_2, \mathbf{u}_3, \mathbf{u}_4\} = \operatorname{rank} N = 3</span></p></div><p>By inspection, we have two linkage classes shown below.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\mathcal{L}_1 = \{\,A,\ 2B\,\}, \qquad \mathcal{L}_2 = \{\,A + C,\ D,\ B + E\,\}, \qquad \ell = 2</span></p></div><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png" width="728" height="289.17953165654814" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:458,&quot;width&quot;:1153,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yxQJ!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47c2d94c-e932-4620-81bb-894f635c747a_1153x458.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>The deficiency of this network is given by subtracting 2, the number of linkage classes, and 3, the dimension of the stoichiometric subspace, from 5, the number of complexes. This gives us a deficiency of zero.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\delta = n - \ell - s = 5 - 2 - 3 = 0</span></p></div><p><span>And it's easy to check that the reaction network is weakly reversible. The deficiency zero theorem then tells us that we only have </span><strong>one positive equilibrium</strong><span> per stoichiometric compatibility class. This is a </span><strong>super cool</strong><span> statement, because the original mass action kinetics for Feinberg's first network look really complicated and messy!</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
\dot c_A &amp;= -k_1 c_A + k_{-1} c_B^{2} - k_2 c_A c_C + k_{-2} c_D + k_4 c_B c_E \\
\dot c_B &amp;= 2k_1 c_A - 2k_{-1} c_B^{2} + k_3 c_D - k_4 c_B c_E \\
\dot c_C &amp;= -k_2 c_A c_C + k_{-2} c_D + k_4 c_B c_E \\
\dot c_D &amp;= k_2 c_A c_C - k_{-2} c_D - k_3 c_D \\
\dot c_E &amp;= k_3 c_D - k_4 c_B c_E
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><p>Let's check our previous network</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>B \xrightarrow{k_1} A, \qquad A + 2B \xrightarrow{k_2} 3B</span></p></div><p>In our example, we found that stoichiometric compatibility classes could contain zero, one or two equilibria. It has deficiency 1.</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\{\,B,\ A,\ A + 2B,\ 3B\,\}, \qquad n = 4</span></p></div><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\mathcal{L}_1 = \{\,B,\ A\,\}, \qquad \mathcal{L}_2 = \{\,A + 2B,\ 3B\,\}, \qquad \ell = 2</span></p></div><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\delta = n - \ell - s = 4 - 2 - 1 = 1</span></p></div><p><span>Similarly for the Michaelis–Menten system </span><sup>[29]</sup><span>, we have</span></p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>E + S \;\underset{k_{-1}}{\overset{k_1}{\rightleftharpoons}}\; ES \;\xrightarrow{k_2}\; E + P</span></p></div><p>Our complexes are</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\{\,E + S,\ ES,\ E + P\,\}, \qquad n = 3</span></p></div><p>Our reaction vectors are</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\begin{aligned}
ES - (E + S) &amp;= \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -1 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \\[1ex]
(E + S) - ES &amp;= \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \\[1ex]
(E + P) - ES &amp;= \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
\end{aligned}</span></p></div><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\text{in the order } (E,\ S,\ ES,\ P)</span></p></div><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>s = \dim \operatorname{span}\left\{ \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -1 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}, \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \right\} = 2</span></p></div><p>And we can count the linkage classes below</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\mathcal{L}_1 = \{\,E + S,\ ES,\ E + P\,\}, \qquad \ell = 1</span></p></div><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png" width="728" height="267.52270327349527" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:348,&quot;width&quot;:947,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!onJ0!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F174cdd57-dee1-482d-a0f3-6a84a7b2d572_947x348.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>This means that our deficiency of this network is given by</p><div data-component-name="Latex"><p><span>\delta = n - \ell - s = 3 - 1 - 2 = 0</span></p></div><p>However, it's not weakly reversible because E+S ultimately reacts to E+P, but E+P doesn't ultimately react to E+S. And so, it can't have an equilibrium concentration that is strictly positive in all its components.</p><p>Here is a table of the deficiencies of other chemical reaction networks we've talked about!</p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png" width="728" height="712.9896907216495" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/ef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:1710,&quot;width&quot;:1746,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:728,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!dPeD!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fef148587-16ac-4a2c-b5bb-8f986299bc78_1746x1710.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p>I hope this piece provides some tools to reason geometrically about chemical systems. My next experiments aim to test some of these theorems physically.</p><p><span>To internalise this content even more, my approach was to get Claude to repeatedly drill me on different kinds of chemical reaction networks. I intentionally added a chapter on vocabulary to practice my muscle memory on picking out features like linkage networks, complexes and stoichiometric subspaces. I wrote a quiz </span><a href="https://claude.ai/artifact/MrpAUjgAN81KFwHTQjkAzZ">here</a><span>, and if you want a deeper intuition I suggest you try some of the problems!</span></p><div><figure><a target="_blank" href="https://substackcd