t&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pwxp!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd869b87e-a945-4bab-a293-bd7d99180d22_941x990.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pwxp!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd869b87e-a945-4bab-a293-bd7d99180d22_941x990.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pwxp!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd869b87e-a945-4bab-a293-bd7d99180d22_941x990.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pwxp!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd869b87e-a945-4bab-a293-bd7d99180d22_941x990.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><em><span>Thank you to </span><a href="https://www.livingphysics.org/">David Jordan</a><span> for continued support.</span></em></p><p>[1] Build-a-Cell. "Synthetic cells 101". https://www.buildacell.org/101 (accessed 2026-11-10).</p><p><span>[2] Feinberg, M. (2019). </span><em>Foundations of Chemical Reaction Network Theory</em><span>. Applied Mathematical Sciences, vol. 202. Springer, Cham. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-03858-8</span></p><p><span>[3] Belousov, B. P. (1959). "A periodic reaction and its mechanism". </span><em>Sbornik Referatov po Radiatsionnoi Meditsine za 1958</em><span>, 145–147. Medgiz, Moscow. Zhabotinsky, A. M. (1964). "Periodic processes of malonic acid oxidation in a liquid phase". </span><em>Biofizika</em><span> </span><strong>9</strong><span>, 306–311. Field, R. J., Körös, E. &amp; Noyes, R. M. (1972). "Oscillations in chemical systems. II. Thorough analysis of tempor