<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div>  <p>I’m <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autism">normal</a>.
This means I have a backlink monitor for this website.
By pure chance, I was showcasing this to a friend when, suddenly, I got a new backlink:</p>
<!-- YES I VIBED THE STYLING FOR THIS. IF YOU FIND A LIBRARY LIKE https://discord-components.js.org BUT UPDATED FOR MODERN DISCORD I CAN USE INSTEAD, PLEASE LET ME KNOW, PLEASE. JACK.CAB/#SOCIALS --><center data-astro-cid-sdsv4kmg=""> <div role="article" data-astro-cid-sdsv4kmg=""> <p><img alt="" src="data:image/webp;base64," data-astro-cid-sdsv4kmg=""></p>  </div> </center>
<p>I tap in,<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-phone" id="user-content-fnref-phone" data-footnote-ref="true" aria-describedby="footnote-label">1</a></sup> forgetting that this is a website, and thus could log my IP or
even contain the <a href="https://blog.mozilla.org/en/firefox/privacy-security/defending-patch-gap/">3-day</a><sup><a href="#user-content-fn-fx" id="user-content-fnref-fx" data-footnote-ref="true" aria-describedby="footnote-label">2</a></sup>
exploit chain of doom. I’m greeted with this:</p>

<p>I sent an early draft of this article to <a href="https://clazite.pages.dev/">another friend</a>, who happens to be Vietnamese, and he told me there’s five casino spam sites ahead of me, which I already knew because I’m Faviconese.
I have the most popular personal website on .cab,<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-rankings" id="user-content-fnref-rankings" data-footnote-ref="true" aria-describedby="footnote-label">3</a></sup> but that’s probably because I have the only personal website on .cab.</p>
<p>I try some other TLDs. Rebane has the #1 .horse, synth.download is the 11th .download, whatever.</p>

<p>Redacted? I hover over it and discover it goes to <code>windows.net.siterate.org</code>.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-resolve" id="user-content-fnref-resolve" data-footnote-ref="true" aria-describedby="footnote-label">4</a></sup> Figuring out the pattern of redactions is not the topic of this article.</p>
<p>I try .com.</p>

