<p>I used a chatbot to convert four screenshots to HTML + CSS, to make the article responsive:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://claude.ai/share/d50c0338-3c8a-454d-a74f-c47bd96db9ca">Removed CSS from <code>http://siterate.org/css/commons.css</code> that wasn’t being used in its tables</a>. Then I handcrafted artisan jackslop: I copied and pasted the tables from the site, changed the <code>[domain].siterank.org</code> links to easter eggs since they don’t resolve, and made the favicons have a stable size and load lazily. For the .com ranking, a friend gave me the idea of annotating the table, which I implemented by hand.</li>
