ked.</p><p>Bloody amazing! Thanks :)</p><h4 id="soe-moe-thu-on-april-3rd-2014"><strong>Soe Moe Thu</strong> on April 3rd, 2014</h4><p>This tricked really worked for me. Thx a lot!!!</p><h4 id="chen-on-april-15th-2014"><strong>chen</strong> on April 15th, 2014</h4><p>This guy put this key solution “He then had me unplug the AC adapter and take out the battery. Then, you push the power button 10 times in a row at one second intervals. Next, you push and hold the power button for 30 seconds. Then you put the battery back in and push the power button… and she lives” WORTH 1000,000 THANKS !!!</p><h4 id="anthony-on-april-17th-2014"><strong>Anthony</strong> on April 17th, 2014</h4><p>worked on my B575e what does it do, some kind of reset.
